'''Araucarians''' are the people who come from the [[Balisca|Baliscan]] [[Communities of Balisca|community]] of [[Araucaria]]. During the colonial period, it became synonymous with the term '''Satanazes''', and centuries later, due to its historical relationship with the [[W:Maroons|Maroons]], with the Araucarian interior being the cradle of their emerging society, the term '''Maroon''' also came to serve as a synonym to designate them; the Araucarian territory, likewise, came to be known as the [[Maroon Confederacy]]. The population is known for its rich diversity of cultural, linguistic and religious manifestations, with the interior of Araucaria being the place of origin of the [[Sureño culture]] (including the [[Araucarian dialect]], cuisine, and [[Lucumí Tarica]]), and its coastline, the cradle of the Sureño culture.

